\label{lem:inheritsetup}
    Suppose that ${\mathcal T}$ is a cluster-tilting subcategory of ${\mathcal E}_{\mathcal P}$.   
    If ${\mathcal E}$ satisfies \Cref{setup:algebraicsetup}\ref{ks}-\ref{fg} then so does ${\mathcal T}$.

\label{thm:noloopsand2cycles}
    Let ${\mathcal T}$ be a cluster-tilting subcategory of ${\mathcal E}_{{\mathcal P}}$ and suppose that ${\mathcal E}$ satisfies \Cref{setup:algebraicsetup}\ref{ks}-\ref{fg}.

    Then the quiver of ${\mathcal T}/{\mathcal P}$ has no loops and no $2$-cycles.

\label{C:Noloops2cycles}
      Let $R$ be a finite-dimensional Gorenstein $\Bbbk$-algebra and $\opname{GP}_{{\mathcal P}}(R)$ be a Frobenius exact structure on $\opname{GP}(R)$, such that $\ul{\opname{GP}}_{{\mathcal P}}(R)$ is $2$-Calabi--Yau.

